 "text": "Hello there, how are you? Great enthusiasm. The key is really simple, think rather than say. Your guests are usually more than happy to tell their story. Start with something simple, like, 'and what was going through your mind?' Or, 'and what was in the room with you?' Not before the interview, up twenty four hours. At the start, yes, but don't send them ahead, they can give guests an edge. You' welcome. Just keep it simple, and let your guest do the talking.",
